# Abe's WorkLouder Creator Micro Studio for Windows.
#
# The working tree is CRLF on disk (Windows editors, Visual Studio) and LF in
# the repository. `eol=crlf` makes Git store LF in the blobs and check out
# CRLF, so the tree stops reporting every file as modified after a Windows
# tool re-saves it. Without this, a checkout and the repo disagree about line
# endings and `git status` shows the whole tree as changed.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Scripts keep the line ending they run with on Windows; PowerShell accepts
# both, so CRLF is safe here too.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Git hooks must stay LF so the shell can execute them on every platform.
/.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be converted.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
